# tools/al/ales_crush_witness.rish — the bit-crusher: drop the low bits, the first DRIVE map that is not odd (ALES81).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES81.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260814/20260814-211634_fill-ales81-lotus-bit-crush.md
# Stands on: lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip, sample_min/max, the one true saturate). No pre-gain and no ceiling — the purest DRIVE member; a
# keeper who wants a boosted crush runs lotus/drive.rye (ALES78) then crush over the same span, both in-place span maps that compose.
#
# lotus/crush.rye shapes RESOLUTION where the sibling drives shape AMPLITUDE. Clearing the low 16−bits bits of a two's-complement integer is
# flooring toward −∞ onto the grid of step 2^(16−bits): q = divFloor(x, step)·step. That floor is why the bit-crush is the DRIVE family's FIRST map
# that is NOT odd — a negative sample floors DOWN, away from zero (crush(−100,8) = −256 while crush(100,8) = 0), a faint downward DC offset that is
# bit reduction's honest fingerprint. The selftest proves it: bits = 16 is the identity; drop-the-low-bits by hand at bits 8 step 256 (255→0,
# 256→256, 500→256, −1→−256, −257→−512); the one-bit floor yields a two-level output {0, −32768}; every output lands on a multiple of the step and
# the map is IDEMPOTENT; the rail is preserved (sample_min fixed, sample_max floors to 32512 at bits 8, every output in range under any bits); the
# map is not odd, the DC signature stated positively; the span discipline holds; a zero or over-wide resolution refuses BadBits, a span past the end
# BadRange, each leaving the clip untouched. The grid lands every output in [sample_min, sample_max] BEFORE the write, so the shape does the bounding
# and the saturate is a documented no-op. Purely local — one divide, one multiply per sample; no pre-gain, no delay line, no dither, no
# anti-aliasing, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device, no real sample rate.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_crush_witness.rish

say "ales-crush: Language EN — the hard clip (ALES78), the overdrive (ALES79), and the wavefolder (ALES80) all shape AMPLITUDE while holding the sample's RESOLUTION: every one of the 65,536 i16 codes still crosses. The bit-crusher shapes the other axis — it drops the low bits, so a signal entered at sixteen bits leaves at eight, four, or one: the coarse, gritty, quantized voice of an early sampler, a lo-fi drum machine, a digital signal starved of resolution."
say "ales-crush: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively as a recognition: DROPPING THE LOW BITS FLOORS TOWARD NEGATIVE INFINITY, so the bit-crush is the DRIVE family's FIRST map that is NOT odd. Clearing the low 16−bits bits of a two's-complement integer is flooring onto the grid of step 2^(16−bits); a negative sample floors DOWN, away from zero, and that faint downward DC offset is bit reduction's honest fingerprint rather than a flaw to hide. bits = 16 is the identity, the crush that crushes nothing."
say "ales-crush: Lens TAME — one mono clip of i16 PCM crushed in place over a span; q = divFloor(x, step)·step with step = 2^(16−bits), exact over the signed integers; the grid includes sample_min and every reachable grid point sits at or below x, so the output lands in [sample_min, sample_max] BEFORE the write, the saturate a documented no-op; the map is IDEMPOTENT (a grid point crushes to itself) and MEMORYLESS (every output depends only on its own input); a resolution outside [1, 16] refuses BadBits, a span outside the samples BadRange, both before any write, the clip untouched on refusal; siloed to lotus/, the resolution a bit count and the grid a power-of-two step in sample units, no pre-gain, no delay line, no dither, no snapshot, no anti-aliasing, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker, no sample rate."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/crush"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/crush.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-crush: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/crush.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-crush: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-crush: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-crush' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-crush: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-crush line"
